h  i'm gonna sit here and go no i'm not  doing anything with you antonio brown  until we find a team that sends us a  first round pick or something like that  because we're losing a ton of money that  we've already invested in you and we  gave you a longer leash than we probably  should have uh to begin with and now  we're stuck in this situation because of  that we're not going to let you just  yell and scream and get your way out of  town  he's banking on the steelers wanting to  turn the page on the drama and the  dysfunction and what he's doing is he's  trying to add to it he took to twitter  on saturday and he offered to answer 10  questions and the first answer was the  most telling he was asked about the  source of his conflict with quarterback  ben rothsberger and he said there's no  conflict just a matter of respect mutual  respect he has an owner mentality like  he can call out anybody including  coaches players know they can't say  anything about it otherwise their meal  ticket is gone it's a dirty game within  a game so yeah he's talking about  the lack of respect that ben  roethlisberger has for the other players  the fact that he feels like he's an  owner and can say what he wants to say  and he's just trying to stir this up and  he's trying to make this conflict  between him and rothersburg to the point  where rothersberger says look it's him  or it's me i don't want the guy here and  there was an interesting  twist that happened on friday afternoon  chris somebody pointed out to me that  antonio brown on his likes and twitter  where you can click that little heart  and you can like a tweet he had liked a  couple of tweets that referred to  roethlisberger's sexual assault  allegations from years ago and there  they were prominent at the top of  antonio brown's likes now he since has  unliked one of them but the message is  clear he's trying to stir it up as best  he can to give the steelers no choice  but to say we can't have this guy around  it's too