ing  us back that 11.4 million dollars are we  on the same page yeah even if we aren't  this is how it's going to be yeah it  seems like it could go that way uh it  definitely does i just wonder what the  compensation they're looking for that  would justify him and justify trading  him and getting him out the door you  know i mean obviously a first round pick  i think that would get it done but are  they to the point where you know if it's  a high second round pick something like  that are they gonna are they gonna flirt  with that to just you know kind of fold  fold the cards and say we're out of the  antonio brown business i wonder what the  price will be to finally make the move  or at least have the deep conversation  about trading antonio brown chris  whatever it is they're not there yet no  because we know we're in that we're in  that window where we we can find out  right that there's a deal in place for a  player that becomes official on march  13. we found that out last week when joe  flacco tentatively was traded from the  ravens of the broncos so if somebody had  given the steelers enough that they  would say yes it would already be done  even though it can't officially be done  yeah until the middle of march  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports

